Okay, if I had a REAL LIFE wand of wishing, I know I'd wish to be on the
NetHack Dev team, but oh well.


Here's the idea. Hell in NetHack is comprised of 30 or so levels of
mazes, with every staircase headed up.

If you've read Dante's Inferno, you'll know why I think Hell should be
only 9 levels of mazes, each maze becoming smaller in area size and
with walls impossible to dig into or teleport around.

Catches:

When you enter Hell, from the lowest point on NetHack by stepping onto
a portal, it would read:

You come to an archway --more--
The archway reads: --more--
"Abandon hope, all ye who enter here!" --more--
The archway disappears behind you as you go through.

You WOULD need fire protection entering the first level of Hell, after that,
Fire protection would be not needed, rather when you descend to the next
level:

Strangely, it feels nice and cool down on this level.

Then, around the 6th or 7th level, you will need cold protection, otherwise.

It's so cold down here, you shiver in your armor. --more--
Your arms stiffen --more--
YOUR ARMS JUST SHATTERED OFF YOUR BODY! --more--
Your legs become numb with cold --more--
YOUR LEGS SHATTER --more--
The rest of your body stiffens with frostbite --more--
Well, at least your corpse won't go bad, being preserved in this cold! --more--
You die (Cryogenically preserved for a future game! ;) --more--

And the death sequence.

And on the scores list, it would read:

"Locnar freeze-dried on the 7th level of Hell" ;)

Otherwise, you just feel cold all over.

No monster un-accustomed to cold lives below 7. That scratches out all
dragons except white ones. Monsters you WILL find would be Ice devils,
and ice trolls.

When you reach the 9th level, there will only be one monster to contend
with.

                              -----
                             /     \
                            /       \
                           /         \
                           |    &    |
                           |    @    |
                           \         /
                            \       /
                             \     /
                              -----

& represents Lucifer, tame Demon Lord, HP 300, SP 200, Gold 0.

As Dante wrote, Lucifer was sent to the 9th level of Hell, there he
found himself encased from the chest down in solid ice, which he cannot
free himself from. Lucifer will see you descend to his level and:

Lucifer says: "Psst, hey, buddy! Could you help me out, please?"

If the player tosses Lucifer a pick-axe or a wand of fire, then Lucifer
takes the pick-axe or wand and frees himself from his icy prison.

Lucifer says: "I will be in your debt forever for your gratitude!"
"If thou will bring me the Amulet of Yendor, I will grant thee a kingdom!"
"For now, to continue thy quest, I grant thee passage back to your world!"

He disappears, and there, lo and behold is a portal to acsend back to
Level one of the Dungeon!

A good idea would be NOT to try and kill Lucifer. ;)

If you recover the Amulet and go back DOWN to the 9th level of Hell,
and toss Lucifer the Amulet, the game will end the same way it would
if you acsend to the EndGame level.

Lucifer rejoices in possesion of the Amulet of Yendor! --more--
Lucifer grants you immortality --more--
You become the new Lord of Hell! --more--

and your game ends with the score reading:

"Locnar descended to become the new Lord of Hell"

What else? Oh yeah.

When you enter Hell, the only way out is on 9.
There are no upstairs to the previous level. Only one way, DOWN!
You can't level teleport.
You can't dig around the walls of Hell, and you can't dig pits in the floor.
and, you can't pray to your god for assistance. ;)

I suppose it's a valid idea. Maybe someone will care enough to work it in.

